# [LISP](../wg/lisp.html)

## Summary

The Locator/ID Separation Protocol (LISP) Working Group met at IETF 127. The session covered working group document status, updates on standards-track and experimental drafts, real-world deployment experiences from managed service providers and enterprise manufacturing environments, and emerging use cases including AI network infrastructure, AI agent communications, EVPN interconnection, and silent host discovery.

---

## Key Discussion Points

### Working Group Document Status
* **Chairs' Update**: Presented by Padma Pillay-Esnault and Luigi Iannone ([LISP WG Chairs Slides](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-lisp-lisp-wg-chairs-slides-00)).
  * The LISP Geolocation specification has been published as an RFC.
  * `draft-ietf-lisp-yang` and `draft-ietf-lisp-nat-traversal` are actively progressing.
  * `draft-ietf-lisp-map-server-reliable-transport` is approaching Working Group Last Call (WGLC).
  * `draft-ietf-lisp-ecdsa-auth` requires addressal of directorate review comments.
